    "body": "Closing: per discussion with Ryan, the global completion flag is intentional — it guards against lazy hydration, which is unsafe in Solid's model (event replay, serialized-data lifetime, DOM drift between load and a late claim). Later roots should hydrate eagerly at load; anything lazier should be a resume mechanism rather than a late hydrate.",
